{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791239178,"nonce":"hRRuuarv3QCzaNuifMqTuUaI/X8=","title":"Canvas drawing allocates heavily per frame: text paths are rebuilt and tessellated every frame","message":"A canvas redraws every frame it changes, and each shape is rebuilt in Haxe from scratch: a new Path and its commands, then Flatten, then Tessellate into the frame's mesh. The garbage this makes sets the GC heap's high-water mark, and the process footprint follows it.\n\n**Measured on tools/demo/Canvas2D.hx** (12 cards, 24 short strings, panned 1 px a frame, Ash hybrid, M-series Mac, 2026-10-05):\n\n- before: about 3.8 MB allocated per frame with the dot background; 780 MB footprint after 16 drags\n- the dot background was about 3 MB of that (about 2,000 circles). Fixed: Brush.pattern draws dots, lines and crosshatch in PathShader, one rect per frame\n- Library.use rebuilt the 517-rule components sheet on every call (once per component part). Fixed: it builds once\n- after: 855 KB a frame, 515 MB footprint after the same 16 drags\n- of the 855 KB, text is about 670 KB and about 8 ms a frame. The board without text is 182 KB and 6 ms\n\n**Remaining: text.** DrawContext.text makes GlyphOutlines.path(outline, x, y), a new offset path per string per frame, and CanvasPainter flattens and tessellates it again each frame. Options:\n- cache the tessellated mesh per (path, linear part of the transform), and add only the translation when the mesh is appended. Panning then re-tessellates nothing. Text would draw a cached path at the origin under a translate, instead of building an offset path.\n- draw canvas text from the glyph atlas as quads, as UI text is drawn (see the text-rendering goals: keep it sharp when zoomed).\n\n**Idle baseline**, for comparison: Interactions idles at 169 MB (126 MB of it native MALLOC_SMALL); Canvas2D idles at about 300 MB. The extra is 40 MB more MALLOC_SMALL, 30 MB of GC heap, 66 MB of GPU (surfaces, toolbar backdrop layers, the canvas data texture) and 21 MB of MALLOC_LARGE. Not yet broken down further.","files":null}]}